STATEMENT OF INTENDED PURPOSE

The following is a statement of the purpose for which this software was
built. It is not a licence term, adds no condition or restriction to the MIT
licence above, and does not modify it.

This software is a research and educational instrument. Its intended purpose
is to demonstrate and teach an informatics method: calibrating a simplified
single-compartment approximation against published pharmacokinetic models of
unfractionated heparin, under simulated conditions. It is not intended for
clinical use, for the care or management of any patient, or to determine,
inform or influence any drug dose.

Within that intended purpose the software is not a medical device.

Nothing in this software has been cleared, approved or evaluated by any
regulatory authority. Its outputs have not been validated against measured
anti-factor Xa activity, activated clotting time or clinical reversal in
patients, and no clinical benefit has been demonstrated. Anyone using it
outside the intended purpose stated above does so on their own responsibility
and may bring the tool within medical-device oversight in their jurisdiction;
the authors accept no responsibility for such use and make no assessment of
how any jurisdiction would classify it.
